        "id": 1961270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-08T17:43:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thats an interesting question. A lot of tL2CAP_LE_RESULT_CODE stuff touches the LE AUDIO stuff which actually uses a different l2cap state (L2CAP_CREDIT_BASED_CONNECTION_RSP) or something like that where as L2CAP COC over BLE as well as L2CAP over BR/EDR all use L2CAP_CONNECT_REQ ore something like that. \n\nCleaning this up including the state machine might be a cleaner code but considering this is more urgent from an Android U perspective adopted a way that is less interfering with anything else.",
      "parentUuid": "72bd630a_82989af9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "de9e6fc2fdebb3a90e83f7faf2a8082e78722566",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "554fb181_0d1ead33",
        "filename": "system/stack/include/l2cdefs.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-08T17:47:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I only see a few usages, and I feel like it\u0027s adding to the mess instead of making things clearer.\n\nMaybe a compromise would be to make the error codes maskable, so that these error codes are 512 + the existing ones.\n\nL2CAP_CONN_INSUFFICIENT_AUTHENTICATION \u003d 512 + L2CAP_LE_RESULT_INSUFFICIENT_AUTHENTICATION\n\nOr something like that.  Then it would be easy to convert back and forth.",
      "parentUuid": "9dc4c36c_fa5d5b2e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "de9e6fc2fdebb3a90e83f7faf2a8082e78722566",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
